Unless... the engine requires the header name to be exactly "Idempotency-Key" (the canonical name) to recognize the idempotency pattern! The expert workflow note said use `req.headers.get("idempotency-key")` — lowercase. Hmm, but maybe the engine's idempotency rule pattern-matches on the header name string. That's plausible for a static proof: the idempotent spec might be discharged only when the run key comes from a recognized idempotency header. The example uses "Idempotency-Key". Let me check if there's a rule about this. Search rules for "idempotency" might help — but search_rules didn't work earlier (returned describe_rule-style empty?). Actually the earlier search_rules returned `payload.rules: []` — maybe because search_rules expects a query that matches rule names.

